From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:14:08 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 082/230] Verify both Telegram signature readings so logins
 stop landing as Guests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bot API 8.0's `signature` field is folded into the signed string by live
Telegram payloads, but the verifier excluded it, so authentic logins were
rejected with `reason=hash mismatch` and silently downgraded to a guest
account; both readings are now accepted (each still demands a bot-token HMAC,
so nothing unsigned gets in). Sign-out also clears the local credential before
the revoke round trip, so a stalled /auth/logout can no longer strand the user.

